WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.359
The Elves and the Shoemaker

00:00:03.059 --> 00:00:10.215
A shoemaker, through no fault of his own, had become so poor that he had nothing left but leather for one pair of shoes.

00:00:10.865 --> 00:00:14.217
That evening, he cut out the shoes he would make in the morning.

00:00:14.567 --> 00:00:18.897
Then, with a clear conscience, he went quietly to bed and fell asleep.

00:00:19.547 --> 00:00:25.243
He slept soundly all night long, never dreaming of the wonderful surprise the morning would bring.

00:00:25.893 --> 00:00:31.035
In the morning, when he sat down to work, the two shoes stood quite finished on his table!

00:00:31.385 --> 00:00:34.226
He was astounded, and did not know what to say.

00:00:34.876 --> 00:00:37.388
He picked up the shoes to look more closely.

00:00:37.738 --> 00:00:44.265
They were so neatly made that there was not one bad stitch in them, just as if they were meant to be a masterpiece.

00:00:44.915 --> 00:00:50.728
Soon a buyer came in, and the shoes pleased him so well that he paid more for them than was usual.

00:00:51.078 --> 00:00:55.472
With the money, the shoemaker was able to buy leather for two pairs of shoes.

00:00:56.122 --> 00:01:01.138
He cut them out that evening, and went to bed with fresh courage, eager for the morning.

00:01:01.788 --> 00:01:04.510
In the morning, the two pairs were already made!

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:09.862
Buyers came gladly and paid him well, so he bought leather for four pairs of shoes.

00:01:10.512 --> 00:01:11.806
And so it went on.

00:01:12.156 --> 00:01:21.073
Whatever he cut out in the evening was finished by the morning, and soon he had his honest independence again, and in time became a wealthy man.

00:01:21.723 --> 00:01:31.734
Now, one evening not long before Christmas, the shoemaker said to his wife, "What do you say if we stay up tonight, to see who it is that lends us this helping hand?"

00:01:32.384 --> 00:01:34.158
His wife liked the idea.

00:01:34.508 --> 00:01:39.970
She lit a candle, and they hid themselves behind the clothes hanging in the corner, and watched.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:43.257
At midnight, two tiny little men came in.

00:01:43.607 --> 00:01:55.927
They sat down at the shoemaker's table and began to stitch and sew and hammer so skillfully and so quickly with their little fingers that the shoemaker could not turn away his eyes for astonishment.

00:01:56.577 --> 00:02:02.995
The next morning his wife said, "The little men have made us rich, and we really must show that we are grateful.

00:02:03.345 --> 00:02:11.504
I will make them little shirts and coats and trousers, and knit them each a pair of stockings, and you shall make them two little pairs of shoes."

00:02:12.154 --> 00:02:21.114
When everything was ready, they laid the pretty little clothes on the table instead of the cut-out leather, and hid themselves to see what the little men would do.

00:02:21.764 --> 00:02:24.052
At midnight the elves came bounding in.

00:02:24.402 --> 00:02:27.222
They found the little clothes and were overjoyed.

00:02:27.572 --> 00:02:39.477
They dressed themselves in the greatest delight, singing, "Now we are boys so fine to see, why should we longer cobblers be?" Then they danced and skipped right out of the door, and never came back again.

00:02:39.827 --> 00:02:43.190
But as long as the shoemaker lived, all went well with him.
